[36m(TaskRunner pid=353998)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=353998)[0m Let's represent \(z\) in its polar form. Since \(|z| = 4\), we can write \(z = 4e^{i\theta} = 4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)\). Then \(\frac{1}{z} = \frac{1}{4}e^{-i\theta} = \frac{1}{4}(\cos\theta - i\sin\theta)\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=353998)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=353998)[0m Substituting \(z = 4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)\) and \(\frac{1}{z} = \frac{1}{4}(\cos\theta - i\sin\theta)\) into the expression, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=353998)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=353998)[0m (75 + 117i)z + \frac{96 + 144i}{z} = (75 + 117i)4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta) + \frac{96 + 144i}{4}(\cos\theta - i\sin\theta).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=353998)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=353998)[0m Expanding this, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=353998)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=353998)[0m (75 + 117i)4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta) + \frac{96 + 144i}{4}(\cos\theta - i\sin\theta) = 4(75\cos\theta + 117i\cos\theta + 75i\sin\theta - 117\sin\theta) + \frac{1}{4}(96\cos\theta - 144i\cos\theta + 96i\sin\theta + 144\sin\theta).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=353998)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=353998)[0m Combining like terms, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=353998)[0m \[
