[36m(TaskRunner pid=353998)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=353998)[0m 4(75\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta) + \frac{1}{4}(96\cos\theta + 144\sin\theta) + i\left(4(75\sin\theta + 117\cos\theta) + \frac{1}{4}(144\cos\theta - 96\sin\theta)\right)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=353998)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=353998)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=353998)[0m The real part of the expression is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=353998)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=353998)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=353998)[0m 4(75\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta) + \frac{1}{4}(96\cos\theta + 144\sin\theta) = 300\cos\theta - 468\sin\theta + 24\cos\theta + 36\sin\theta = 324\cos\theta - 432\sin\theta
[36m(TaskRunner pid=353998)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=353998)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=353998)[0m To find the maximum value of \(324\cos\theta - 432\sin\theta\), we can use the fact that the maximum value of \(a\cos\theta + b\sin\theta\) is \(\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}\). So, the maximum value of \(324\cos\theta - 432\sin\theta\) is \(\sqrt{324^2 + 432^2}\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=353998)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=353998)[0m Let's calculate this value using Python.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=353998)[0m ```python
[36m(TaskRunner pid=353998)[0m import math
[36m(TaskRunner pid=353998)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=353998)[0m # Coefficients
[36m(TaskRunner pid=353998)[0m a = 324
[36m(TaskRunner pid=353998)[0m b = -432
[36m(TaskRunner pid=353998)[0m 
